        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Oakley, Kansas\n- Buildings: Oakley High School Stadium, Irwin Stadium, Irwin Field\n- Organizations: Works Progress Administration\n- Concepts: New Deal works programs, KHRI# 109-51, 2010 census\n\nFacts:\n- The Oakley High School Stadium in Oakley, Kansas was built in 1939 by the Works Progress Administration as part of a New Deal works program.\n- The Oakley High School Stadium is also known as Irwin Stadium, Irwin Field, and KHRI# 109-51.\n- The 2010 census recorded the population of Oakley, Kansas as 2,045.",
